===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|North America|Philippines}} A [[final examination]]; a [[test]] or [[examination]] given at the end of a [[term]] or [[class]]; the test that concludes a class.
#: {{ux|en|I've barely squeaked through my '''finals'''.}}
#* {{RQ:WaPo|date=13-04-2005|author=Robert MacMillan|title=Steal This Song|url=http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/articles/A49361-2005Apr13.html|accessdate=3 Oct. 2008
|passage=It was tough cramming for those midterms and '''finals''', staying up 72 hours straight hepped up on caffeine and pizza.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251106211941/https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/articles/A49361-2005Apr13.html|archivedate=6 November 2025}}
# {{lb|en|Oxbridge slang}} A final examination taken at the end of the final year of an [[undergraduate]] course, which contributes towards a student's [[degree]] [[classification]].
# {{lb|en|sports}} The last [[round]], game or match in a contest, after which the winner is determined.
# {{lb|en|phonology}} The final part of a [[syllable]], the combination of [[medial]] and [[rime]] in [[phonetics]] and [[phonology]].
# {{lb|en|music}} The [[tonic]] or [[keynote]] of a [[Gregorian mode]], and hence the final note of any conventional melody played in that mode.

